WEBVTT

1
00:00:02.000 --> 00:00:07.500
<v Nadia Farouk>Morning. Let's scope the support ticketing tool. First, how does a ticket get created?</v>

2
00:00:08.000 --> 00:00:13.000
<v José García>A user submits a ticket with a title, a description, and a priority of Low, Medium, or High.</v>

3
00:00:13.500 --> 00:00:16.000
<v Nadia Farouk>Understood. What happens to a High priority ticket?</v>

4
00:00:16.500 --> 00:00:21.000
<v José García>A High priority ticket is auto-assigned to the on-call engineer immediately.</v>

5
00:00:21.500 --> 00:00:27.000
<v José García>First response targets: High is four hours, Medium is one business day, Low is three business days.</v>

6
00:00:27.500 --> 00:00:31.000
<v Nadia Farouk>Noted. Does the person who raised the ticket get told about progress?</v>

7
00:00:31.500 --> 00:00:36.000
<v José García>The requester gets an email on every status change of their ticket.</v>

8
00:00:36.500 --> 00:00:40.000
<v>Can a closed ticket be reopened later?</v>

9
00:00:40.500 --> 00:00:44.000
<v José García>Yes, a requester can reopen a closed ticket at any time.</v>

10
00:00:44.500 --> 00:00:49.000
<v Nadia Farouk>Hold on, I thought a ticket locks seven days after it's closed and can't be reopened.</v>

11
00:00:49.500 --> 00:00:52.000
<v José García>We may be misaligned on that. Let me check with the team.</v>

12
00:00:52.500 --> 00:00:55.000
<v Nadia Farouk>Okay. How was your holiday, by the way?</v>

13
00:00:55.500 --> 00:00:58.000
<v José García>It was great, thanks. Let's keep going.</v>

14
00:00:58.500 --> 00:01:02.000
<v Nadia Farouk>That's a good start. We'll pick up next week.</v>
